 with Toby Love. Later releases include «Secreto», «Loca» and «Demos Paso Al Amor», the live album «Judy Santos Live», recorded in a virtual performance during the pandemic quarantine, and «All By Myself», with Wilmore “Bimbo” Franco. In May 2021 she released «No Me Rendiré», co-written and produced by the Grammy winner Chris Hierro, with a video directed by Iván Castillo, and distributed by «La Oreja Media Group»; she said the audience chose it through a poll, and it reached number 24 on Billboard’s Tropical Airplay chart that year.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Back with Aventura","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"On 9 October 2021 she reunited with ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"3a7c19e8-5d24-4f06-b8e1-9c4a70f2d5b3","displayText":"Aventura","occurrenceId":"6bc32edf-02f6-47c7-961a-a6eea93fc19a"}},{"text":" at MetLife Stadium to sing «Obsesión» at the group’s final concert of its reunion tour.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Legacy","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"On 10 July 2026 she released «Tócame el alma», a romantic bachata written with Eddie Espinal and produced by Erickson Zavala. Diario Libre reported that on 9 August she would be the only artist representing bachata on the main stages of the SummerStage festival in New York, after a 2026 in which she also performed the show «Una Dosis De To’» in New York and gave a special presentation for students at Boston College.","type":"text"}]}]}'::jsonb, 'published', id, 1 FROM artists WHERE slug = 'judy-santos';
